codex
Concrete execution exposed a semantic issue before proof work: K’s generated strictness machinery evaluated the condition but left the reconstructed `If` stuck. I’m replacing that generated mechanism with four explicit branch rules—one true/false pair for each parameter—so the semantics itself states exactly how string equality controls a Python `if`.
apply patch
